        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-20 21:08:55.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21279 lov: keep the objects of an unknown pattern",
        "message": "LU-21279 lov: keep the objects of an unknown pattern\n\nA client that read a layout with an instantiated component whose\npattern it did not know would read past the end of its lov stripe md\nentry in lov_lsme_pack_v1v3(), and oops if it found NULL there, e.g.\nfor getxattr(\"lustre.lov\"), since lsme_unpack() allocated no\nlsme_oinfo[] for such a component, but kept its stripe count and INIT\nflag, and the packing still walked its objects.  lsme_free() and\ndump_lsm() skipped them as unpacking did.\n\nKeep the objects of such a component in lsme_unpack(), without\nlooking up their OSTs, since no IO uses them, so that the layout is\npacked with them and a copy of it keeps them, and free and dump them\nas for any other component.  An unknown pattern with the MDT bit, as\nLOV_PATTERN_BAD has, is not taken for Data-on-MDT when unpacking.\n\nAdd sanity-flr test_62b to check that the layout of a written mirror\nwith an unknown pattern keeps its objects.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-flr\nFixes: 14ed4a6f8f23 (\"LU-16837 llite: handle unknown layout component\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I0035a3df20e889d048452217dbc6cc0e733ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
